The temp SVG element appended to `document.body` on line 69 is only removed at line 92, with no `try/finally` guard. If `configureLabelImages()`, `getBoundingClientRect()`, or any intervening operation throws an exception, `tempSvg.remove()` is never called and the hidden `<svg>` element remains in the document permanently, leaking DOM nodes across every label render that encounters an error. Wrap the block in a `try/finally` block to ensure cleanup:
```js
try {
  await configureLabelImages(div.node(), node.label);
  let bbox = div.node().getBoundingClientRect();
  // ...
} finally {
  tempSvg.remove();
}
```

`getClusterTitleWidth` is a synchronous function calling async `createLabel` without `await`. The `label` variable holds a `Promise`, not a DOM element, so `label.getBBox()` on line 491 will throw or return meaningless results. While this was a pre-existing issue, this PR is modifying the call signature of this line and should take the opportunity to fix the root cause. `getClusterTitleWidth` needs to be made `async` and the call needs an `await`:
```js
export const getClusterTitleWidth = async (elem, node) => {
  const label = await createLabel(node.label, node.labelStyle, undefined, true, false, node.width);
  // ...
};
```
All callers will need to be updated accordingly.

`hasKatex(node.label)` is called without a null/falsy guard, whereas the original code checked `node.label && hasKatex(node.label)`. While `node.label` is coerced to `''` earlier in `createLabel`, `addHtmlLabel` is a separate function that could be called independently. The original defensive guard should be preserved:
```js
const sanitizedLabel = node.label && hasKatex(node.label)
  ? await renderKatexSanitized(...)
  : sanitizeText(node.label, config);
```
